# 5. CORS, Same-Origin API Routing and Trusted Proxy

CORS must be configured correctly for the actual deployment topology.

## 5.1 Preferred architecture: Same-origin public routing

The recommended arrangement is:

- Browser loads `https://techa.ir`.
- Browser API calls use the same public origin.
- IIS routes `/api/*` to the Express backend.
- IIS routes `/api-docs*` to the Express backend.
- Next.js server-side data fetching can call Express through its private loopback address.

Under this architecture, browser requests to `/api/...` are same-origin.

They do not need cross-origin CORS permissions merely because Express uses a different internal port.

## 5.2 Explicit CORS allowlist

