# 18. Security and Operational Constraints

- Never commit real `.env` files.
- Never embed credentials in PM2 configuration.
- Never use wildcard credentialed CORS.
- Never expose MongoDB credentials to Next.js client bundles.
- Never trust all forwarded proxy headers without a known topology.
- Never expose raw internal service ports publicly by default.
- Never hardcode `62.220.123.21` as the browser-facing website URL.
- Never generate the OpenAPI server URL from arbitrary untrusted request headers.
- Never fabricate Swagger endpoints.
- Never publish internal diagnostic information.
- Never execute production database modifications as part of deployment tests.
- Never make destructive changes to IIS or Windows Firewall automatically.
- Never claim remote server setup is finished when it has only been documented.

